      "text": "Epilepsy clinic letter\nConsultation: 01 March 2025\nPatient: Christopher Vance, aged 29\n\nDear colleague,\n\nChristopher is a 29-year-old gentleman with an established diagnosis of generalized epilepsy. He has been taking levetiracetam 1000 mg twice daily with excellent reported adherence. He has been entirely seizure-free for over fourteen months, with his last generalized tonic-clonic convulsion occurring on 10 January 2024. He reports no myoclonic jerks or daytime absences.\n\nWe agreed to maintain his levetiracetam dosage. No changes or investigations are indicated. Next review in three months.\n"
    }
  ],
